     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>21-Year-Old Tirupati Student Builds AI Ecosystem for Video Creation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Innovation</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Startup</span> <span>#Technology</span></div>
       <p>Kosinepalli Arjun Sai, a 21-year-old Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning graduate from Mohan Babu University in Tirupati, is pioneering an AI-powered ecosystem called AatonovaZ Technologies Pvt Ltd. This student-led startup aims to revolutionize video production for creators, particularly those working independently, by integrating filming, editing, and multilingual dubbing into a seamless workflow.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/21-year-old-tirupati-student-builds-ai-ecosystem-for-video-c.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The genesis of AatonovaZ began in 2023, during Arjun’s first engineering semester, when he faced the challenge of finding a Telugu-dubbed version of the film Swades. This personal experience led to the conception of JusDub, an AI-powered multilingual dubbing tool designed to overcome language barriers. Recognizing that dubbing was just one facet of a complex production process, Arjun expanded his vision to create a comprehensive &quot;cyber-physical ecosystem&quot; where physical devices and AI software collaborate.</p><p>AatonovaZ currently features three flagship products. GarudaOne is a smart drone that responds to voice commands, including in Indian languages like Hindi and Telugu, to capture footage while performing obstacle avoidance. Editra, an AI video editor, automates the assembly of raw footage, adding music and transitions, capable of drafting an hour-long video in 10 to 20 minutes, complete with AI-generated, copyright-free music. JusDub, Arjun’s initial innovation, translates videos while meticulously preserving the speaker's original emotions.</p><p>This innovative approach has garnered significant attention, including Rs 20 lakh in pre-seed funding under the Startup India Seed Fund Scheme. Arjun’s journey was significantly supported by mentorship at Mohan Babu University, with figures like Yudhish Jain and Dr Padmaja aiding in refining his ideas. AatonovaZ has also achieved global recognition, ranking among the Top 25 teams in Samsung Solve for Tomorrow and winning ANVESHAN 2025–26. Currently in validation, the startup aims to commercialize its tools, aspiring to create &quot;the iPhone for content creators.&quot;</p><p>Why it matters: This innovation democratizes video creation, empowering independent creators with advanced, integrated tools.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive and well-structured report that captures the key details, figures, and products from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/youth/young-innovators/ai-content-platform-startup-arjun-sai-mohan-babu-university-tirupati-aatonovaz-technologies-12681156" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
