     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Approximately 76% Voter Turnout Recorded in Nagaon Lok Sabha Bypoll</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Approximately 76% of roughly 19.05 lakh electors cast their votes during the Nagaon Lok Sabha constituency bypoll in central Assam on Tuesday. State election officials stated that the final percentage is expected to rise since voters inside polling stations before 5 p.m. were permitted to vote. Fifteen candidates contested the seat, featuring a primary race between BJP's Devasish Sharma, Congress's Sibamoni Bora, and AIUDF chief Mohammed Badruddin Ajmal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/approximately-76-voter-turnout-recorded-in-nagaon-lok-sabha-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The election was triggered after Pradyut Bordoloi shifted from Congress to the BJP. Barring a minor confrontation over alleged vote-switching in Juria, voting remained largely peaceful, with vote counting scheduled for October 9.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate representation of the bypoll turnout and key candidates.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/assam/about-76-voter-turnout-in-nagaon-lok-sabha-bypoll/article71552134.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
