     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Cockroach Janta Party Criticises Maharashtra Police Over Notices Issued to Workers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijit Dipke criticized the Maharashtra Police on Tuesday for allegedly serving notices under Section 168 of the BNSS to party workers. The notices allegedly advise workers to avoid the upcoming October 10 protest at Jantar Mantar against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar and inquire about their travel fund sources.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/cockroach-janta-party-criticises-maharashtra-police-over-not.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Mr. Dipke condemned the action as dictatorship, claiming similar notices were issued in Rajasthan. Despite the police pressure and allegations that the agitation would be violent, the CJP affirmed that it will move forward with the planned protest.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the core details and quotes without introducing outside facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/cjp-activists-getting-police-notices-being-pressured-not-to-join-october-10-delhi-protest-abhijit-dipke/article71550853.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
