     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Police Detain Protesters Amidst Debate on Constitutional Dissent</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Delhi Police and paramilitary forces detained approximately 150 protesters outside Connaught Place as authorities restricted demonstrations at the denotified Jantar Mantar site. Security forces utilized barricades and preventive custody under Section 163 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita to manage crowds gathering to unfurl the national flag. The crackdown sparked intense debate among political analysts and leaders regarding the boundaries of constitutional dissent, democratic rights, and the legitimacy of regime change rhetoric.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/delhi-police-detain-protesters-amidst-debate-on-constitution.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Demonstrators, including citizens concerned about corruption and unemployment, vowed to continue their silent movement despite ongoing detentions. While BJP representatives defended the police measures as necessary to address obstruction of duty, opposition figures and activists argued the protests remained within constitutional parameters.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Correctly conveys detention numbers, legal references and the debate among politicians.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/regime-change-row-sanjay-jha-charu-pragya-yashvardhan-azad-debate-protests-ytvd-3019189-2026-10-16?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-16/delhi-police-detain-protesters-amidst-debate-on-constitution" data-title="Delhi Police Detain Protesters Amidst Debate on Constitutional Dissent"><b>Share:</b>
