     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Former Selector Chetan Sharma Urges BCCI for Balanced Pitches</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former chief selector Chetan Sharma has called on the BCCI to provide more supportive wickets for bowlers during international matches. His remarks follow the ongoing India-West Indies T20I series, where batters have dominated, frequently posting totals exceeding 200 runs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/former-selector-chetan-sharma-urges-bcci-for-balanced-pitche.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sharma emphasized that while fans enjoy boundaries, healthy competition requires balanced surfaces similar to those used in domestic cricket. Additionally, he defended the inclusion of veterans Rohit Sharma and Virat Kohli in the national setup, asserting that their performance remains the primary metric for selection ahead of the 2027 ODI World Cup.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Succinctly captures the former selector's stance on pitch conditions and his defense of veteran players.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/bcci-sent-urgent-plea-by-ex-chief-selector-chetan-sharma-on-bowlers-behalf-ahead-of-5th-india-vs-west-indies-t20i-12192717#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
