     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India Faces West Indies in T20I Series Decider at Chinnaswamy</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>India hosts the West Indies on October 17, 2026, at M. Chinnaswamy Stadium for the fifth and deciding T20I, with the series currently tied at 2-2. This marks the ninth T20I for India at the Bengaluru venue, where they hold a record of four wins, three losses, and one no-result.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/india-faces-west-indies-in-t20i-series-decider-at-chinnaswam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India has batted first in all eight previous T20I matches at this ground, winning all four instances where they set a target. The venue has a history of high-stakes finishes, including a dramatic double Super Over victory against Afghanistan in 2024 and narrow wins against Bangladesh and Australia.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is dense and correctly synthesizes the source data.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/what-is-indias-t20i-record-at-m-chinnaswamy-stadium-bengaluru/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
