       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka Chief Minister D.K. Shivakumar Leaves for New Delhi Ahead of GST Council Meeting</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Karnataka Chief Minister D.K. Shivakumar traveled to New Delhi on Tuesday ahead of the 57th GST Council meeting scheduled for October 8. Sources indicate the visit could offer an opportunity to meet senior Congress leaders to discuss pending matters, including State Cabinet vacancies, Legislative Council appointments, and board nominations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/karnataka-chief-minister-dk-shivakumar-leaves-for-new-delhi-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>However, discussions remain uncertain as senior Congress leaders, such as Lok Sabha Opposition Leader Rahul Gandhi, are occupied with protests against the ECI. During a previous visit last week for a Congress Working Committee meeting, Mr. Shivakumar met Union Ministers to address drought situations, development projects, irrigation schemes, and fund releases for Karnataka.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: All facts, figures, and attributions align precisely with the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/karnataka/karnataka-chief-minister-leaves-for-delhi-ahead-of-gst-council-meeting/article71551971.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/new-delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">New Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
