       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Karnataka High Court Rules on Pharma License Suspension</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Karnataka High Court has ruled that pharmaceutical distributors must be granted a fair hearing before authorities can suspend their drug licenses. The decision followed a challenge by Wellness Forever Chemists against a September 2026 suspension notice.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/karnataka-high-court-rules-on-pharma-license-suspension.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Emphasizing due process, the court permitted the distributor to continue business operations while the case proceeds. Certain product restrictions remain in effect as the legal matter is resolved. This ruling reinforces the necessity of providing businesses an opportunity to present their case before punitive administrative actions are finalized.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief captures the core legal development accurately.</p>
