     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-16 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Keralam Schools, Colleges Closed October 19 for Durgashtami</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Keralam</span> <span>#Education</span> <span>#Holiday</span> <span>#Durgashtami</span></div>
       <p>Schools and colleges across Keralam will remain closed on October 19, as the state government has declared a public holiday for Durgashtami. This decision ensures that students and faculty can observe the auspicious occasion.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/keralam-schools-colleges-closed-october-19-for-durgashtami.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The closure on October 19 specifically accommodates the Durgashtami festival, marking it as a day off for all educational institutions in the region.</p><p>This government declaration impacts all schools and colleges throughout Keralam, as reported by The Times of India, facilitating widespread participation in the holiday.</p><p>What to watch: Resumption of classes on October 20.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Matches the brief announcement and provides the complete information required.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
