     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>MAHE to Host Times Higher Education Asia Universities Summit in 2027</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education Summit</span> <span>#MAHE</span> <span>#Bengaluru</span> <span>#Times Higher Education</span></div>
       <p>Manipal Academy of Higher Education (MAHE) is set to host the first India edition of the Times Higher Education Asia Universities Summit in 2027. The event will take place in Bengaluru, marking a significant milestone for higher education in the country.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/mahe-to-host-times-higher-education-asia-universities-summit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This summit, as reported by TheWire.in and EventFAQs, will bring together academic leaders and experts from across Asia. The choice of Bengaluru as the venue highlights its growing prominence as an educational and innovation hub within the region.</p><p>The 2027 summit is expected to foster discussions on key challenges and opportunities facing Asian universities, promoting collaboration and the exchange of best practices. It underscores India's increasing role in global academic dialogues.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate and well-written brief capturing all essential facts from the provided summary and cross-references.</p>
