     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ramayana: Part 1 International Trailer Unveiled in Bengaluru</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Ramayana</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Trailer</span> <span>#Film</span></div>
       <p>The international trailer for &quot;Ramayana: Part 1,&quot; directed by Nitesh Tiwari, was officially unveiled in Bengaluru on October 15. This event marks the commencement of Sony Pictures’ global campaign to introduce Namit Malhotra’s ambitious adaptation of the Indian epic to international audiences. The launch was attended by key cast and crew members, including Ranbir Kapoor, Sai Pallavi, Yash, Ravi Dubey, composer A. R. Rahman, and director Nitesh Tiwari.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/ramayana-part-1-international-trailer-unveiled-in-bengaluru.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Hosted by Prime Focus Studios and Yash’s Monster Mind Creations, the nearly two-and-a-half-minute preview offered a fresh look at the film, presenting the story on an expansive fantasy scale centered on a cosmic conflict between light and darkness and a battle against tyranny. The trailer opens in a mythic era depicting men and gods coexisting, with Kunal Kapoor appearing as Lord Indra. The narrative then shifts to the rise of Yash as Ravana, who declares, “Before me, every head will bow,” establishing the central conflict. Ranbir Kapoor is presented as Lord Rama, a righteous figure facing an extraordinary destiny, stating, “If I don’t stop him, the world will fall.” Sai Pallavi as Sita is also glimpsed, hinting at the emotional depth of the story, which emphasizes large-scale battles, ancient architecture, atmospheric landscapes, and visual effects by DNEG.</p><p>The film's score, composed by Hans Zimmer and A. R. Rahman, significantly shapes the trailer's grand presentation, showcasing the makers' vision for the big screen with its blend of mythological setting and large-scale fantasy elements. The cast includes Ranbir Kapoor as Lord Rama, Sai Pallavi as Sita, Yash as Ravana, Sunny Deol as Hanuman, and Ravi Dubey as Lakshman. Produced by Namit Malhotra’s Prime Focus Studios in collaboration with DNEG and Yash’s Monster Mind Creations, the two-part saga is poised for global reach.</p><p>Sony Pictures will spearhead the international campaign and handle global distribution outside India, while Dharma Productions will distribute the film in the Hindi-speaking market. &quot;Ramayana: Part 1&quot; is scheduled for a worldwide theatrical release on November 5, 2026, in IMAX and multiple Indian languages including Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, and Malayalam. The second installment is slated to arrive during Diwali 2027.</p><p>What to watch: Anticipation builds for the global theatrical release of &quot;Ramayana: Part 1&quot; on November 5, 2026.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is a well-structured summary of the provided source text, capturing all essential details including the release date and key cast members.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ramayana-international-trailer-shares-a-glimpse-of-ranbir-kapoor-as-lord-rama-having-an-epic-face-off-with-yash-as-ravana/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
