     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-16 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sensex and Nifty Trade Higher Amidst Q2 Earnings</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian equity markets traded in a narrow range on Friday, with the Sensex rising 238.38 points to 74,553.99 and the Nifty50 climbing 82.45 points to 23,079.80 by mid-morning. While the Nifty IT index led gains, broader markets saw the Nifty MidCap and SmallCap indices decline by 0.35 per cent and 0.18 per cent, respectively.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/sensex-and-nifty-trade-higher-amidst-q2-earnings.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Investors are currently assessing global cues and ongoing second-quarter earnings reports from major firms like PNB and DLF. Meanwhile, several companies, including Tonbo Imaging India and Zetwerk, continue their initial public offering subscription periods in the primary market.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Correctly reports the market indices and notes the primary market activity and earnings reports.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
