     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Supreme Court Stays Twisha Sharma Death Trial Pending Transfer Consideration</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Supreme Court has stayed the trial in the unnatural death case of model Twisha Sharma, who was found hanging in her Bhopal home on May 12. A bench led by Chief Justice Surya Kant issued notices to the CBI and the accused, husband Samarth Singh and mother-in-law Giribala Singh, regarding a petition to transfer the proceedings to Delhi. The petitioner, Navnidhi Sharma, cited concerns over potential bias and the influence of the accused.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/supreme-court-stays-twisha-sharma-death-trial-pending-transf.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The CBI previously took over the investigation from Madhya Pradesh police, eventually invoking charges of abetment of suicide. While the trial in Bhopal had reached the stage of framing charges, the Supreme Court has halted all proceedings to evaluate the transfer request.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and well-structured, though it omits the specific detail that the petitioner cited the mother-in-law's former status as a district judge as a reason for potential bias.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/twisha-sharma-death-case-supreme-court-stays-bhopal-trial-delhi-transfer-ptag-3018941-2026-10-16?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
