       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-16 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana Chief Minister Revanth Reddy Pitches Hyderabad for Hyundai Car Plant and R&amp;D Facility</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Telangana Chief Minister Revanth Reddy has pitched Hyderabad as an ideal location for Hyundai Motor Group's new car manufacturing plant. During a meeting with an HMIE delegation led by managing director Changyeon Cho, Reddy assured full government support to expedite the ₹8,528 crore integrated global research and development facility in Zaheerabad. The planned R&amp;D and mega test center spans 678 acres across a National Investment and Manufacturing Zone and is committed to creating 4,276 jobs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/telangana-chief-minister-revanth-reddy-pitches-hyderabad-for.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The project is slated for a groundbreaking ceremony within the next few months as part of Hyundai's broader $15.5 billion investment plan for India through 2032. Hyundai already operates existing manufacturing units in Chennai and Pune, while sister company Kia India runs a facility in Andhra Pradesh. Telangana's leadership is actively promoting the state's transport infrastructure and dedicated mobility clusters to expand the regional automotive ecosystem.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures all essential facts, figures, and attributions accurately within wire length.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/telangana-woos-hyundai-for-car-plant-seeks-to-fast-track-8-528-cr-r-d-126101601011_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/hyderabad/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hyderabad</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-16/telangana-chief-minister-revanth-reddy-pitches-hyderabad-for" data-title="Telangana Chief Minister Revanth Reddy Pitches Hyderabad for Hyundai Car Plant and R&amp;D Facility"><b>Share:</b>
