     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · BBC Health · 2026-10-16 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>UK Covid Vaccine Compensation Scheme to Be Reformed Following Inquiry Criticism</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health</span> <span>#UK</span> <span>#Vaccines</span> <span>#Policy</span></div>
       <p>Ministers in the UK have pledged to overhaul the compensation scheme that offers financial support to individuals injured or bereaved due to vaccines. This commitment follows recent criticism emanating from an official Inquiry into the existing provisions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/uk-covid-vaccine-compensation-scheme-to-be-reformed-followin.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The scheme, which provides crucial financial aid, supports those who have experienced adverse effects or suffered bereavement linked to vaccines administered in the United Kingdom. The promised reforms aim to address shortcomings identified by the Inquiry, ensuring more effective support for affected parties.</p><p>What to watch: Details of the proposed reforms and their implementation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate brief summary of the source material, though slightly repetitive in the second paragraph.</p>
