       <h1>Visakhapatnam Madhurawada Residents Flag Civic Issues Ahead of GVMC Polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Ahead of the Greater Visakhapatnam Municipal Corporation (GVMC) elections, residents in Madhurawada have raised concerns regarding unaddressed civic services like roads, drainage, and garbage collection. In Srinivasa Nagar, locals reported that roads dug up by the Electricity Department remain covered in rubble, while gravel unloaded in August lies in heaps and uncollected waste litters roadsides.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-16/visakhapatnam-madhurawada-residents-flag-civic-issues-ahead-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Residents also highlighted issues with unsegregated waste disposal and stagnant water causing mosquito breeding. Meanwhile, Marikavalasa residents stated they have lacked motorable roads for over 40 years, causing severe safety and accessibility hazards during the monsoon season.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Succinct and dense summary of the local grievances ahead of the municipal elections.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/andhra-pradesh/residents-in-visakhapatnams-madhurawada-flag-poor-roads-drains-ahead-of-gvmc-polls/article71593517.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
